Difference between class and struct.
 - A class is a reference type, while a struct is a value type.
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------|
|                                | Class                           | Struct                           |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Type                           | Reference type                  | Value type                       |
| Represents                     | Usually an entity/object        | Usually a value                  |
| Assignment                     | Copies reference                | Copies value                     |
| Can have methods               | ✅                              | ✅                              |
| Can have properties            | ✅                              | ✅                              |
| Can implement interfaces       | ✅                              | ✅                              |
| Inheritance from another class | ✅                              | ❌                              |
| Can inherit another struct     | ❌                              | ❌                              |
| Default value                  | `null`                          | Zero/default values              |
| Typical use                    | `Customer`, `Order`, `Employee` | `Point`, `DateTime`, small value |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------|


